# ProxyAPI adapter rules

- ProxyAPI integration exists only inside provider/infrastructure adapters.
- Never expose the ProxyAPI key to frontend code.
- Keep base URL, API key, timeout and model mapping in validated server configuration.
- Treat ProxyAPI responses as external untrusted data and validate critical fields.
- Prefer actual charged cost returned/reconciled from provider data when reliably available; preserve enough usage detail to audit derived cost.
- Implement provider balance monitoring as corporate treasury/observability, separate from user allowance.
- Low ProxyAPI balance must never be interpreted as a user's balance.
- Design for future fallback to another provider without changing billing, chats or frontend contracts.
- Use separate development/production credentials and provider-side budgets/IP restrictions when available.
